+\paragraph{Complete conditional existence boundary (Block 24).}
+The eleventh block established the corresponding conditional matrix criterion.
+Block 24 now uses the complete common-spine conclusion of Claim 8.2: the returned
+coefficient-field representations are continuous, have the prescribed common
+polynomials and coefficient-specific determinants, and satisfy every selected
+local realization relation under the stated inverse-limit closure hypothesis.
+All finite reductions belong to the admissible classes.
+
+For each supplied required packet $p$, let $A_p$ be its finite-dimensional carrier
+over a characteristic-zero field $E_p$, and let $e_p$ be the actual joint spectral
+projector for its finite list of split commuting conditions. No order on $E_p$
+is assumed. The source notation $\Tr(e_p)>0$ means that the unique natural number
+$n_p$ with $\Tr(e_p)=(n_p:E_p)$ is positive. The checked projector formula identifies
+$n_p$ with the dimension of the actual joint eigenspace.
+
+An admissible realization here includes continuous coefficient-field members and
+membership of every finite reduction in its designated admissible class.
+Under the completion hypotheses and these supplied carrier hypotheses, Lean proves
+\[
+\begin{aligned}
+&\exists\,\rho,\ (x_p)_p:\quad
+  \rho\text{ is an admissible realization of the full chosen spine},\quad
+  0\ne x_p\in\operatorname{im}(e_p)\text{ for every }p\\
+&\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad
+ \bigl(\forall\lambda,\ X_{\lambda,1}(\Compat)\ne\varnothing\bigr)
+ \ \land\ \bigl(\forall\lambda,\ \forall m\ge2,
+               X_{\lambda,m}(\Compat)\ne\varnothing\bigr)
+ \ \land\ \bigl(\forall p,\ n_p>0\bigr).
+\end{aligned}
+\]
+The packet index may be infinite. Each $x_p$ belongs to its own supplied carrier;
+no common vector across distinct carriers or embedding of the reconstructed
+system into those carriers is asserted. Neither an unknown carrier nor positive
+trace is constructed without the corresponding hypotheses.
